INSTALL

Ubuntu with an NVIDIA GPU:
1. Install the NVIDIA driver and the CUDA toolkit from the NVIDIA website,
   or with: sudo apt install nvidia-cuda-toolkit
2. Install build tools and python: sudo apt install build-essential python3
3. Verify with: nvcc --version and nvidia-smi
4. Build with: make
5. Generate data with: python3 src/generate_data.py
6. Run with: bash run.sh

Google Colab (no local GPU needed):
1. Create a notebook and set the runtime to a GPU.
2. Upload src/edge_detect.cu and src/generate_data.py.
3. Run: !python3 src/generate_data.py then
   !nvcc -std=c++11 -O2 src/edge_detect.cu -o edge_detect -lcudart then
   !./edge_detect -i data/input -o data/output
